{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>To the midwife.</b> It is of the root מוֹלִידוֹת — except that some are קַל and some are כָּבֵד, like שׁוֹבֵר and מְשַׁבֵּר, דּוֹבֵר and מְדַבֵּר — so too מוֹלִיד and מְיַלֵּד." "<b>Shifrah.</b> Yocheved — after the name that she beautifies (מְשַׁפֶּרֶת) the child (ibid.)." "<b>Puah.</b> This is Miriam — for she cries out (פּוֹעָה) and speaks and croons to the child (ibid.), in the manner of women who soothe a crying infant." "<b>Puah.</b> A term of crying out, as in ״כַּיּוֹלֵדָה אֶפְעֶה״ (Isaiah 42)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:10.634370172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}